		"description": "The `portal` property key over HTTP (change a-property-says-what-the-portal-may-do-with-it, task 2.1): one case per scenario of the spec.\n\nA request with an X-Portal-Subject header is made on behalf of a resident. For it, the objects API leaves out every property whose portal is none or absent, on reads and on the object a write answers with, and refuses with 403, naming the properties, a write that would change a property that is not edit. The same calls without the header are unchanged, and that is asserted too.",
